# Sourced, not run. The holder the Developer ID certificates are issued to, as each
# certificate's name ends: "Developer ID Application: <holder>" signs the bundles and
# "Developer ID Installer: <holder>" signs the package. [LAW:one-source-of-truth] The team in
# the parentheses is what every signature is held to, so it is written here and nowhere else.
# notarytool takes the team alone, beside an Apple ID.
developer_team=6R988MUU27
developer_id="Brandon Fryslie ($developer_team)"
# The authority both certificates are issued under: Apple's G2 Developer ID intermediate, as
# served at https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/DeveloperIDG2CA.cer. macOS does not
# carry it, and a signature has to chain through it.
developer_id_ca="$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/DeveloperIDG2CA.cer"
